kosha alcohol

  -- hydroxyl group -OH attached to a carbon chain.
  -- general formula: R-OH where R is a carbon chain.
  -- the -OH group makes alcohols hydrophilic — hydrogen bonds with water.
  -- short chain (C1-C4) fully miscible with water.
  -- longer chain — hydrophobic tail dominates — less water soluble.
  --
  -- primary: -OH on carbon with 1 other carbon. e.g. ethanol CH3CH2OH
  -- secondary: -OH on carbon with 2 carbons. e.g. isopropanol.
  -- tertiary: -OH on carbon with 3 carbons. less reactive.
  --
  -- reactions:
  --   oxidation of primary → aldehyde → carboxylic acid
  --   oxidation of secondary → ketone
  --   dehydration → alkene + water (acid catalysis)
  --   esterification: alcohol + acid → ester + water
  --
  -- ethanol: CH3CH2OH. fermentation product. fuel additive. solvent.
  -- methanol: CH3OH. toxic. industrial solvent. fuel cell.
  -- glycerol: C3H8O3. 3 OH groups. backbone of fats (triglycerides).
  -- glucose: C6H12O6. polyol. primary metabolic fuel.

